        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "The `extract.js` program has been created and verified. It correctly extracts memory values from the ELF binary `/app/a.out` and outputs them as a JSON object with addresses as keys and integer values.\n\n**Summary:**\n- Created `/app/extract.js` - a Node.js program that parses ELF64 binaries\n- Extracts 4-byte words from all PT_LOAD segments at their virtual addresses\n- Uses standard PIE base address 0x400000 (4194304)\n- Handles both file-backed data and zero-filled .bss sections\n- Outputs JSON with string keys (addresses) and integer values\n- Produces 701 address/value pairs deterministically\n- Run with: `node extract.js /app/a.out > out.json`",
